# .trivyignore — trivy rules to silence globally for lint-gitlab-ci-scripts
# https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# Add rule IDs here to suppress false positives inherent to this tool's approach.

# DS-0031: Secrets passed via ENV — false positive: CI predefined variables
# (CI_JOB_TOKEN, CI_REGISTRY_PASSWORD, etc.) are declared as empty ENV
# placeholders so shellcheck does not report SC2154 (undefined variable).
# They do not contain real secrets in the generated Dockerfiles.
DS-0031
